From: miuicamera-cupid
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Add in-app Monet dynamic color switch and disable manual color picker when active

1. com.android.camera.data.data.t.v():
   Check DataItemGlobal boolean "pref_monet_color_key" (default true).
   When enabled, return Global.getApplication().getColor(android.R.color.system_accent1_200)
   (0x0106003b). When disabled, fall through to stock "pref_tint_color" selection
   so all 12 stock colors (including Leica Red) work untouched.

2. CameraCommonPreferenceFragment (Wa, te, onResume, onPreferenceChange):
   Add CheckBoxPreference "pref_monet_color_key" right above "pref_tint_color"
   (localized in pt/en), and automatically call setEnabled(!isMonet) on
   "pref_tint_color" both on screen load and live when toggled.
